A||||2||JetroGT||Fixing Weather Pack connectors||||1||
Z||000000||JetroGT||12-10-2001||08:56 PM||||I saw that the Fiero Store sells the replacement connectors but you have to cut and splice the wires to replace them. <BR> <BR>I had a spare connector laying around and decided to take it apart. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Weatherpack1.jpg"> <BR>First I uncliped the back cover. Then I used part of a telescoping antenna to depress the barbs on the wire end and slid it out. Now I can replace all my broken connectors without cutting one wire. I'll have to take a trip to the junk yard tommorow to get some good connectors.  <BR> Thanks for the space<BR><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NewSigt.jpg">   <BR>I work where all the missing paperclips go.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||12-10-2001||09:40 PM||||Hey Jetro!<BR>You can buy NEW pins, sockets, and shells at NAPA and many other stores...<BR>Also, they have the extractor to pull the sockets and pins...<BR>You may need to shop around electronic supply stores for the crimper, or try Snap-on...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||JetroGT||12-10-2001||10:04 PM||||I may as well buy new shells then. Forget the junk yard.<BR>Thanks!||||reg||10
